    "id": "l1_cross_quotient_split_descent_obstruction",
    "title": "L1 cross-quotient split-descent obstruction",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "An exact F_23 maximal chart with ell=2, five two-point petals, one background point, fixed petal polarity p=5, and two saturated threshold contributors has cross quotient 16+9X+4X^2+15X^3=(X-13)(20+15X+15X^2). The quadratic discriminant 14 is nonsquare, so the quotient is not split. The cell has N=8,d=4,h=5 and N(2d-h)=24>=16=d^2, placing the obstruction in the live sub-Johnson tail. Cross-quotient injection therefore cannot be iterated as split-defect descent without an additional splitting theorem.",
